{
 "id": "ridgeline-coy-attack",
 "title": "Op RIDGELINE — company attack (sample)",
 "mapId": "ridgeline",
 "turns": 16,
 "minutesPerTurn": 4,
 "weather": "clear",
 "timeOfDay": "day",
 "firstSide": "blue",
 "briefing": {
  "situation": "Red Land forces have occupied the ridge north of the Lower Jhelum Canal with an infantry company (-) reinforced with an IFV, machine guns and anti-tank weapons. Their positions are dug in on Pt 252 and around the village of Kotli Sharif. A small outpost watches the main road bridge over the canal. Red is expected to defend in place and counter-attack locally. Red artillery (122 mm) is likely to be available from about turn 3.",
  "mission": "A Coy (reinforced) is to capture Kotli Sharif and Pt 252 by the end of turn 16, in order to secure the line of the ridge for the battalion advance.",
  "forces": "Own: A Coy — Coy HQ, 1 Pl and 2 Pl (three rifle sections each), 3 Pl (mechanised: two sections in APCs), MMG and ATGM teams, 60 mm and 81 mm mortar sections, sniper and recce teams, a mini UAV and a troop of two tanks. In support: one 155 mm battery, 4 missions from turn 2 (one-turn delay). Enemy: infantry company (-) with an IFV, MMGs, HMG, ATGM, RCL and RPG teams and an 81 mm mortar section, supported by a 122 mm battery.",
  "time": "16 turns of about 4 minutes each, by day, weather clear. Blue moves first.",
  "victory": "Objectives: Kotli Sharif (5 VP), Pt 252 (3 VP), Canal bridge (1 VP) — all held by Red at the start. At the end of turn 16 the side holding the greater objective value wins (Red wins a tie). Red wins at once if A Coy falls below 35 % of its strength; A Coy wins at once if Red falls below 30 %.",
  "lessons": [
   "Use the woods south of the ridge as a covered approach",
   "Suppress before you move: fire and manoeuvre",
   "Do not let vehicles cross open ground in view of ATGMs",
   "Use the observer rule: mortars and guns need eyes on the target",
   "Reverse slopes protect the defender from long-range fire"
  ]
 },
